# Jak 1 intro, the boat shot timed (LIST-0.1.6 item 21; the owner on a Quest 3: a stutter "only ... for that short
# shot of him laying back on the boat"). jak1_intro_boat.sim with three shots only (pictures slow the run): the cut to
# him lying back, where the intro first shows Misty Island ("Displaying level misty", "Setting force-all-visible?[misty]
# to #t": the island drawn whole), is at about frame 5090 to 5430 (the loads move it). Run with JAKVR_FRAME_TRACE=8
# JAKVR_BUCKET_LOG=1: "[vr-frame]" lines name the game frames over 8 ms of work (none there in 0.1.6's runs), "[vr]
# bucket" lines each renderer as it starts drawing (Misty's plants, l0-shrub, about 91,000 triangles at the cut).
